baoc - C compiler for BaOS ELF executables

Description:
Compiles C source to ELF32 i386 programs linked with crt0 and the BaOS libc.
Supports preprocessing (#include, #define, #if), functions, globals, switch,
extern/libc symbols, structs, pointers, and multiple source files.

Usage:
  baoc input.c output
  baoc [-o output] file1.c [file2.c ...]

Examples:
  baoc /programs/hello.c /programs/hello
  baoc -o /programs/app /programs/a.c /programs/b.c

Requires on disk: /lib/crt0, /lib/libc, /lib/baoc_syms, /lib/include/*.h

Tests (under /test on the filesystem after make):
  test1-test4: core language
  test7: printf + libc
  test8: globals
  test9: switch
  test10: multi-file (compile test10_helper.c and test10.c together)
  test11: cast, sizeof, hex
  test12: array initialization
